Let a frontend with no window read and change a profile's settings by getConfig()'s keys

An app with its own settings screen needs to show what a profile's settings are, not only set them: runLua() answers
only whether the code ran, so an app could push setConfig() calls but never read a value back, and a script that put
its own getConfig in the globals would answer for Mudlet.

- THeadlessSession::settings(keys, values) calls Mudlet's own TLuaInterpreter::getConfig for each key, with true for
  its second argument so an option of several comes as its name, and gives each as a bool, a double or a QString. A
  key getConfig() does not know, or that gives a table or nothing, is left out.
- THeadlessSession::setSettings(values, refused) calls TLuaInterpreter::setConfig for each, so events and the save
  behave as for a script's setConfig(), and gives back each key it refused with the message setConfig() gave, its Lua
  error for a value of the wrong type, or that the value was not a bool, a number or a string.
- Both are false, reading or changing nothing, where runLua() is refused.
- docs/headless.md describes them.
- getConfig() and setConfig() gain six keys an app's settings screen needs, each a bool kept with the profile:
  sslIgnoreExpired, sslIgnoreSelfSigned and sslIgnoreAll (the certificate errors a secure connection lets past),
  acceptServerGUI and acceptServerMedia (whether the game may install its packages and play its media), and
  echoLuaErrors (a script's errors also shown in the main console). The getConfig() table lists them too.
- They also gain serverEncoding, the game's text encoding as getServerEncoding() and setServerEncoding() read and
  change it: by the names getServerEncodingsList() gives, ASCII for none, kept with the profile as the preferences'
  encoding is, and refused with setServerEncoding()'s message for a name Mudlet does not have.
- And the input line's three, kept with the profile as the preferences' Input line tab keeps them: commandSeparator
  (the text a sent line is split at, none when empty), highlightHistory (a command brought back from the history is
  selected whole) and disablePasswordMasking (no hidden-input box when the game hides what is typed).
- And the console's colours, as #rrggbb text kept with the profile as the preferences' Color view tab keeps them: the
  sixteen ANSI ones by the names color_table gives them (ansiBlack to ansiLightWhite), foregroundColor,
  backgroundColor, commandForegroundColor and commandBackgroundColor. A change refreshes the console's colours and
  color_table as the preferences' does, so text decoded after it takes it; anything not #rrggbb is refused. Beside
  them serverMayRedefineColors (the game may redefine the sixteen), enableOSC8Hyperlinks (OSC 8 links are shown and
  advertised) and alertOnNewData (the new text alert), each a bool.

Tested in HeadlessSessionTest (reading, a script's replacement getConfig, an unknown key, a change taken and three
refused, the refusals with no profile, the encoding refused, changed and read again by a new session, the input line's
three changed and read again by a new session, and a colour refused, then colours and the display's three changed,
the background reaching consoleColorsChanged, and read again by a new session), and the new keys in Other_spec.lua.
The desktop's preferences are unchanged.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

